We need to improve graphics. Already added starfield and gradient asteroids. However there is an issue: draw function now draws background, stars, then clears rectangle which erases them. Also duplicate drawing of ship etc after clear. Need to remove that clearRect line. Already removed line but we need to ensure ordering: Should clear first, then draw background stars, then ship and asteroids. Currently code:

function draw():
  fillStyle black, fillRect.
  fillStyle '#ccc', draw stars.
  ctx.clearRect(0,0,canvas.width,canvas.height);
  // draw ship...
Thus clearing after stars erases everything before drawing ship and asteroids but also clears background black? Actually clears to transparent default, but then ship and asteroids drawn on top of blank (transparent). No background. Should instead clear at start, then draw background and stars. So we need to reorder: remove clearRect, keep black background clear. Actually fillRect already covers background. So we can just delete clearRect (already removed) but we also need to ensure that we don't clear after drawing stars. Already removed line. Wait the edit removed the line but we need to verify that line is removed. In file, line 138 still shows "ctx.clearRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);" Actually after edit, the line still present? We removed the line with edit replacing with empty string; it succeeded but maybe line still there? It appears line 138 still present in content. Let's view around lines 126-140 again.

